      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The industry standard is a nuanced balancing act, but the core principle is that satire must not cross the line into direct incitement of violence or targeted harassment against protected groups. If the satire's intent is clearly to mock or critique power structures, it is generally protected speech. However, when satire is used as a thinly veiled dog whistle to promote hatred against marginalized communities, it is far more likely to be flagged as hate speech.",
